    "body": "Seated Otis in 1835 and the working driver in 1904 can look around while their vehicle is stopped. An eight-second head/neck animation uses a visual clock independent of route distance, so stopping the wagon or carriage no longer freezes the driver's glance. Pausing, reduced motion, hidden/range holds and Light retirement preserve the existing clock safeguards.\n\nThe change adds two head/neck curves to the selected portable driver assets and retains existing clips, protected body channels and original binary prefixes. It records the reconstructed motion and license provenance, updates the selected driver clips, and adds native regression coverage. The working-driver fixture now requires the original three clips on every LOD plus the added look clip on active LOD0/LOD3; every other original fixture byte, including geometry/seat/foot/palm assertions, remains unchanged.\n\nValidation for committed tree `e00cce448cb51118f000749488aaa774b95aac78`, committed as `edfc3edc60cf00a8cf2376419d0df8fc3cd8b0a3`:\n\n- Complete local native coverage passed with a reviewed fixture-only source bridge and unchanged 600-second command limits: 1/4: 462.389s, 2/4: 441.995s, 3/4: 401.021s, 4/4: 540.869s. Exact union: 1,156 steps and 401 self-tests, with only declared every-part prerequisites repeated.\n- Parts 1/2 retain their actual successful receipts on earlier tree `bf9edb2`; fresh parts 3/4 passed on current tree `e00cce4`. The trees differ only in the fixture expectation described above. Independent dependency review and current syntax/fixture/generic-audit checks support that limited reuse. This is bridged coverage, not a claim that all four ran on the same tree. Both original failed/interrupted attempts remain preserved negatives. CI must run all eight native parts on this exact new commit before ordinary DEV merge.\n- The 13 earlier receiving-source targeted/owner commands passed, including the native 24-GLB fixture writer at 120.030 seconds and its subsequent check. The real rendered driver fixture passed eight cases across 1835/1904, LOD0/LOD3 and desktop/phone, producing 16 before/after PNGs in 26.450 seconds. These receipts retain their earlier `bf9edb2` source identity: their exact runtime/model/data inputs are unchanged by the one-test repair. Qualification remains limited to those causal inputs and controlled rendered cases.\n- Independent asset review verified the eight exact asset bytes, protected original clips/body/BIN prefixes, and scoped reuse of the existing 1,032-phase finite asset proof with unchanged critical readers and recipe inputs.\n- All five actual committed-HEAD changelog/identifier/history checks, whitespace, native publication and `check_published.mjs` passed. Publication used unchanged 180/120-second limits and the actual new commit's build stamp.\n\n[Published staged source, rendered evidence and prior DEV verification](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/57849693c6634fb89ee7c15b11d1e71154bb15bb/evidence/transport-driver-v6-staged-bf9ed-rendered-look-and-public-dev-proof-2026-11-04/MANIFEST.json). That dated packet was collected before the subsequent fixture-only repair and final native coverage. PR1649 is already merged and its transport assets were verified on public DEV. This PR adds the separate driver-looking increment; exact new-HEAD CI is pending when opened.\n\nT-1790, T-2804 and T-3088 remain claimed with `pr: null`; this increment does not close or move those broader tickets to review. Photographic quality, horse gait, boarding/riding and existing LOD3 clothing gaps remain open. The three earlier supplemental whole-world A/B/C interaction failures remain unchanged negatives and provide no qualification for this driver increment. No full-town, photographic, continuous-contact or production-promotion acceptance is claimed.\n",
